{"id":"CON-interface","status":"decided","answer":"src/ratings/notch.mjs: RATING_SCALE = the 19 ratings, best first: AAA, AA+, AA, AA-, A+, A, A-, BBB+, BBB, BBB-, BB+, BB, BB-, B+, B, B-, CCC+, CCC, CCC-. notchChange(previous, current) -> integer = index(current) - index(previous) on that scale: positive = downgrade, negative = upgrade, 0 = unchanged; range -18..+18. notchCalculator(previous, current) -> { notches, direction: 'downgrade'|'upgrade'|'unchanged', wl }, notches signed like notchChange (C5), wl: downgrade of 2 -> 1, 3+ -> 2, 1 -> 0 (C2, C6), upgrade/unchanged -> 0 (C3). src/indicators/countryRating.mjs: countryRatingChangeWl(previous, current) -> 0|1|2: downgrade of 1 -> 1, 2+ -> 2, upgrade/unchanged -> 0 (REQ-03-12, C3), built on notchChange. Inputs: rating strings, trimmed and case-insensitive; anything else (including empty string, null, undefined, numbers) -> RangeError (C1). Open sub-points: what 'trimmed' strips (X-trim, business); whether RATING_SCALE is frozen (X-scale-immutability, pm).","source":"JOB.md Contract, C1, C5","quote":"`notchChange(previous, current)` → integer; positive = downgrade, negative = upgrade, 0 = unchanged. … `notchCalculator(previous, current)` → `{ notches, direction: \"downgrade\" | \"upgrade\" | \"unchanged\", wl }` … `countryRatingChangeWl(previous, current)` → 0 | 1 | 2 … is signed exactly like `notchChange` (downgrade positive, upgrade negative)."},
{"id":"CON-errors","status":"decided","answer":"Any input that is not, after trimming and case-folding, one of the 19 ratings of C1 throws a RangeError - from notchChange, notchCalculator and countryRatingChangeWl alike (the latter two propagate notchChange's error). This includes non-string inputs (null, undefined, 5, {}), the empty string, whitespace-only strings, ratings outside the scale ('CC', 'D', 'NR', 'Baa1') and internal spaces ('BBB +'). It must be a RangeError, not a TypeError - calling .trim() on null would naturally throw TypeError, so the implementation must guard for it. No fallback value is returned. The message text is not in the contract (X-error-message, pm).","source":"JOB.md C1","quote":"anything else is rejected with a RangeError"},
{"id":"CON-compat","status":"n_a","answer":"Nothing exists to stay compatible with: the repository has only src/.gitkeep and test/.gitkeep; both modules and all four exports are new. No versioning is asked for beyond package.json 0.1.0.","source":"repo: git ls-files (src/.gitkeep, test/.gitkeep); package.json"},
{"id":"ARC-style","status":"decided","answer":"Library: plain Node ES modules inside the single watchlist-poc package, imported directly by other POC parts. The change lives in src/ratings/ and src/indicators/, with tests under test/.","source":"JOB.md Contract; CLAUDE.md; README.md","quote":"other parts of the POC will import exactly these … Plain Node.js 18+ ES modules … Code lives in `src/<area>/`, tests in `test/<area>/*.test.mjs`."},
{"id":"ARC-components","status":"decided","answer":"One component: watchlist-ratings (kind library, stack javascript/node, paths src/ratings/, src/indicators/, test/), owned by backend and reviewed by reviewer. No service, BFF, app, worker or database (see architecture).","source":"JOB.md Contract; CLAUDE.md","quote":"src/ratings/notch.mjs … src/indicators/countryRating.mjs … files `test/<area>/<name>.test.mjs`"},
{"id":"ARC-layer","status":"decided","answer":"A shared domain library of pure functions (no I/O). Layers that call it (screens, indicator engine) are built later by other parts of the POC.","source":"CLAUDE.md; JOB.md C8","quote":"Pure functions, no I/O in `src/ratings` and `src/indicators`."},
{"id":"ARC-stack","status":"decided","answer":"JavaScript, Node.js 18+, ES modules (.mjs), no framework. No new dependencies of any kind (so no licence question). Tests: node:test + node:assert/strict.","source":"CLAUDE.md; JOB.md","quote":"Plain Node.js 18+ ES modules (`.mjs`). No npm dependencies; do not add any."},
{"id":"ARC-data","status":"n_a","answer":"No data is stored: the functions take two rating strings and return a value. C7 rules out persistence; CLAUDE.md rules out I/O. The rating scale is a constant in code.","source":"JOB.md C7; CLAUDE.md","quote":"no persistence"},
{"id":"ARC-integration","status":"n_a","answer":"No external system is called: fetching the country rating from a public source is out of scope (C4); the caller passes previous and current rating in.","source":"JOB.md C4","quote":"Fetching the rating from a public source is OUT of scope for this slice"},
{"id":"ARC-async","status":"decided","answer":"Synchronous: each function returns its value directly (integer, object, 0|1|2), not a Promise. Pure and deterministic, so no ordering or idempotency concerns.","source":"CLAUDE.md; JOB.md Contract","quote":"Pure functions, no I/O … `notchChange(previous, current)` → integer"},
{"id":"NFR-performance","status":"n_a","answer":"The request sets no latency, throughput or volume target. The work is a lookup in a 19-item constant inside pure, I/O-free functions, so there is no performance risk to manage.","source":"JOB.md (no performance requirement); CLAUDE.md (pure functions, no I/O)"},
{"id":"NFR-availability","status":"n_a","answer":"An in-process library with no runtime dependencies and no I/O: nothing can be down, so there is no degradation path.","source":"JOB.md C4; CLAUDE.md"},
{"id":"NFR-security","status":"decided","answer":"No authentication, authorisation or secrets: these are pure functions with no I/O and no user context. Input validation is the only security concern, and C1 sets it: only the 19 scale ratings (trimmed, case-insensitive) are accepted; everything else throws a RangeError (see CON-errors; what 'trimmed' strips is open in X-trim).","source":"JOB.md C1; CLAUDE.md","quote":"Input is trimmed and case-insensitive (\"bbb+\" = \"BBB+\"); anything else is rejected with a RangeError."},
