{"id":"NFR-audit","status":"decided","answer":"No audit in this slice. Recording who confirmed or edited a pre-filled rating is explicitly excluded.","source":"JOB.md C7","quote":"No override parameter, no persistence and no audit trail in this slice."},
{"id":"NFR-observability","status":"decided","answer":"None: no logging, metrics, tracing or console output. The functions are pure and produce no printed output.","source":"JOB.md C8; CLAUDE.md","quote":"No UI, CLI or printed output in this slice. … Pure functions, no I/O"},
{"id":"NFR-compliance","status":"n_a","answer":"This is a proof of concept, and the request names no regulation or internal policy. The business rules (scale, thresholds, the corrected example) were confirmed by the business unit in C1-C8, so no further compliance constraint shapes this slice.","source":"README.md (proof of concept); JOB.md Clarifications (confirmed by the business unit)"},
{"id":"TST-strategy","status":"decided","answer":"Unit tests with node:test + node:assert/strict in test/<area>/<name>.test.mjs (test/ratings/notch.test.mjs, test/indicators/countryRating.test.mjs), written by the dev; QA checks every AC with node --test. The test data comes from the request's examples (C1, C2, C3, C5, C6) plus edge cases: AAA and CCC- ends, an 18-notch move, invalid and non-string input. No test environment is needed. No coverage number is set (X-coverage).","source":"CLAUDE.md; JOB.md","quote":"Tests: `node:test` + `node:assert/strict`, files `test/<area>/<name>.test.mjs`. `npm test` runs everything."},
{"id":"DEL-ci","status":"decided","answer":"`node --test` (full suite) must pass. There is no lint, typecheck or security-scan tooling in the repo, and none may be added as a dependency. Commits carry no AI attribution (enforced by the gate).","source":".deliver.json; package.json","quote":"\"verify_full\": \"node --test\""},
{"id":"DEL-deploy","status":"decided","answer":"Nothing is deployed. Other POC parts consume the code by importing the ES modules from the repo; there are no feature flags and no migrations, and rollback means reverting the merge.","source":"JOB.md Contract, C8","quote":"other parts of the POC will import exactly these"},
{"id":"DEL-docs","status":"n_a","answer":"The request asks for no documentation, changelog or runbook. The contract section of JOB.md is the interface description for importers, and README.md already describes the layout (src/<area>/, test/<area>/).","source":"JOB.md intro and Contract; README.md"},
{"id":"X-trim","status":"open","question":"C1 says input 'is trimmed' but does not say which characters are stripped. Which whitespace must be removed from both ends before the rating is matched?","options":["A: JavaScript String.prototype.trim() - all Unicode whitespace and line terminators (space, tab, CR, LF, NBSP U+00A0, U+FEFF, U+2000-U+200A, U+3000, ...); zero-width space U+200B is NOT stripped","B: ASCII whitespace only (space, \\t, \\n, \\r, \\f, \\v); NBSP etc. -> RangeError","C: plain spaces (U+0020) only; tabs/newlines/NBSP -> RangeError"],"impact":"Changes which inputs are accepted and which throw a RangeError, for all four exports. Example: 'BBB+\\u00a0' (a non-breaking space, typical when copied from a web page or PDF) is accepted under A and rejected under B and C; '\\tBBB+\\n' is accepted under A and B and rejected under C. QA test data and the edge-case ACs depend on the answer.","owner":"business"},
